# Development / test dependencies — the direct ones, hand-written.
#
# An input, like requirements.in beside it. The file to install is the compiled
# `requirements-dev.txt`, which is the whole graph pinned and hashed:
#
#     pip install -r requirements-dev.txt
#
-r requirements.in

black==26.5.1
mypy==2.4.0
# HTTP client used by starlette.testclient in Starlette 1.x. Pinned at 2.12+
# rather than 2.7: pip-audit flags six advisories against the older line
# (PYSEC-2026-3844..3849), and a dev-only dependency is still a dependency
# CI has to install.
httpx2==2.13.1
pytest==9.1.1
pip-audit==2.10.1
pytest-cov==7.1.0
# The resolver that compiles the two .in files into the two lockfiles. In here
# rather than left to whoever is at the keyboard so that "how do I relock?" has
# one answer, and so CI has the tool it needs to check the lock is in step with
# these inputs — see the "Lockfile" step in .github/workflows/build-deploy.yml.
